1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:09,560
Oh, hi. Hey, you've got to try this cheesecake. Oh, you know, I'm not that much of a sweet tooth.

3
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:19,000
Oh my god, so creamy. Oh my god, that is the best cheesecake I've ever had. Where did you get this?

4
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,640
It was at the front door when I got home. Somebody sent it to us.

5
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:29,300
Chandler, this is not addressed to you. This is addressed to Mrs. Braverman downstairs.

6
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:36,920
Thief. I didn't read the box before I opened it and you can't return a box

7
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:39,880
after you've opened the box. Why not? Because it's too delicious.

8
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:47,460
Chandler, you stole this cheesecake. That is wrong. No, no, no, it is going to be okay

9
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:51,700
because Mrs. Braverman is going to send away for a free one and that way we all

10
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:58,100
win. The only losers are the big cheesecake conglomerate, mama's little bakery.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,600
I feel terrible. I'm a horrible, horrible, horrible person. Well, I'm sorry, what?

12
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:37,120
I'll be there for you.

13
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:50,780
All right, I should get going. Big day at work. You know, I'm in a coma,

14
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:55,360
but today they do this test on me and it turns out I'm not brain dead.

15
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:02,240
Mr. Smarty Pants, it's just my character that's not brain dead.

16
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:07,620
Hey, Sophie, you still on for tonight? Absolutely. I'll see you at eight. Okay.

17
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:13,180
Huh, what's at eight? Oh, I have dinner plans with Joey. We get together about once a month

18
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:20,780
to discuss the rest of you guys. Wow, did not know that. May I say how lovely you look today?

19
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:27,960
Duly noted. Oh, so for tomorrow, do you want to rent a car and drive down together or what?

20
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:34,080
What are you talking about? Because in Franny's wedding, it's tomorrow night. You were invited?

21
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:42,080
No. I can't believe this. I mean, I knew that mom and dad were invited,

22
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:47,080
but I thought that was it. I mean, from the ages of seven to nine, Franny and I were inseparable.

23
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:50,600
Well, maybe since the age of nine, Franny's made some new friends.

24
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:55,280
Do you want to make some new friends?

25
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:00,780
Well, it's probably just a mistake. Let me call Aunt Cheryl, okay?

26
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:04,260
Maybe you are invited and the invitation just got lost in the mail.

27
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:07,600
Yeah, well, you call her and tell her that, you know, when we were kids,

28
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,460
her precious little Franny tried to undress me several times, okay? And if I hadn't stopped her,

29
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,500
there probably wouldn't even be a wedding to go to.

30
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:20,380
She tried to undress me, too. I used to undress my cousin, Glenn,

31
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:31,640
too. Joseph Francis Triviani, are you home yet?

32
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:36,620
Um, I think he's still out. What's wrong? Well, I'll tell you, Rachel Karen Green.

33
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:40,360
I had plans with Joey tonight and he left me this note.

34
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:45,540
Phoebs can't make it. Got a date. Talk to you later. Big Daddy.

35
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:50,240
Big Daddy? Oh, that's a nickname we were trying out.

36
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,920
Why don't you guys try out Francis?

37
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,580
Francis is a cooler name than Chandler, isn't it?

38
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:02,140
You know what nickname never caught on? The Rossitron.

39
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:08,620
Hey. Oh, here's Joseph Francis.

40
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:14,180
What are you middle-naming me for? I left you a note.

41
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:16,780
So what? That doesn't give you the right to ditch me.

42
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:20,300
Hey, you can cancel plans with friends if there's a possibility for sex.

43
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,860
Maybe he's right. That is the rule. Really?

44
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:27,900
Well, that's what I hear. I've never gotten a chance to actually employ the rule.

45
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:33,960
Well, I don't accept this rule. When we make plans, I expect you to show up,

46
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:37,380
okay? I can't just be a way to kill time till you meet someone better.

47
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:41,760
You know, boyfriends and girlfriends are gonna come and go, but this is for life.

48
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:46,760
Wow. I'm so sorry. I had no idea it would bother you this much.

49
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:50,220
Well, it does. Okay, can I make it up to you?

50
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:55,580
I'm sorry. How about dinner tomorrow night? I'll pay for myself.

51
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,640
Okay, you wore me down.

52
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,800
Hey, Joe, while you're over there, how about another beer for the Rossitron?

53
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,180
Oh, is that back?

54
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,560
Hi. Yeah, the cheesecake came.

55
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,900
They delivered it to the wrong address again.

56
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:28,040
So, just bring it back downstairs. What's the problem?

57
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:29,940
I can't seem to say goodbye.

58
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:35,400
Are you serious? Chandler, we ate an entire cheesecake two days ago, and you want more?

59
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,900
I've forgotten what it tastes like, okay?

60
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:45,220
It was cheesecake. It was fine. It had a buttery, crumbly graham cracker crust

61
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:52,200
with a very rich, yet light cream cheese filling.

62
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:57,260
Wow, my whole mouth just filled with saliva.

63
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:02,720
You know what? Forget it. We are just hungry. We have not had lunch.

64
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:08,120
We are just lightheaded. So, let us go out and have lunch and forget about the cheesecake.

65
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:10,220
Yeah, we'll drop it off downstairs so that we're not tempted.

66
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:12,020
Good idea. Where do you want to go to lunch?

67
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:13,680
Mama's Little Bakery, Chicago, Illinois.

68
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:20,560
Oh, Mel Torme died.

69
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:23,720
Joey, that paper's like a year old.

70
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,860
Oh, does that mean the Sam Goody sale is over?

71
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,000
Hey. Hey.

72
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:31,300
Hey.

73
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:36,800
So, I finally heard back from Aunt Cheryl, and apparently it wasn't a mistake.

74
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:39,140
There's limited seating in the hall.

75
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:42,840
Limited seating? I am just one tiny person.

76
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:49,740
Well, yeah, but she doesn't know that. I mean, the last time she saw you,

77
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,700
you would have turned one of those little wedding chairs into kindling.

78
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:58,160
Limited seating? Oh, that is such a lame excuse.

79
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,820
It's the reason why she's not inviting me.

80
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:04,960
What's the big deal? I wasn't even invited to the ceremony, just the reception.

81
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:09,080
And you know what? If it makes you feel any better, Joan and I will just make an appearance,

82
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:12,980
and then we'll leave early as a sign of protest.

83
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:15,860
Joan? Yeah, Joan Tedeschi, my date.

84
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:19,140
She's an assistant professor in the linguistics department. Tall,

85
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:23,860
very beautiful, and despite what some people say, not broad-backed.

86
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:31,360
Wait a minute, you got Ross Geller and guest? I wasn't invited, and you got and guest?

87
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:37,000
Excuse me, I do have to interrupt on Ross's behalf. I think the rule applies here.

88
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,580
You know, since he has a chance to get on broad-backed.

89
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:40,820
Not broad-backed.

90
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,700
Dude, I've seen her. She's like a billboard.

91
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,540
Wait a minute, you know what? You're bringing me.

92
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,640
I can't cancel on Joan.

93
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,360
Why not?

94
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:59,000
Did you not hear me? She's an assistant professor in the linguistics department, okay? They're wild.

95
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:02,260
Why do you want to come anyway?

96
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:10,680
Because. She's my cousin. I mean, we grew up together. Family, and I don't know, that's

97
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,960
important to me.

98
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:17,660
Okay, all right, I'll take you. I'll go call Joan.

99
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:25,020
Oh, that's nice. Family should be there. This is her wedding. Happiest day of her life.

100
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:26,260
We'll see.

101
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,500
Well, thank you for lunch.

102
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:36,100
What? Wait a minute, I didn't pay. I thought you paid.

103
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,400
So apparently, we just don't pay for food anymore.

104
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:42,860
Do you see what I see?

105
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:43,860
It's still there.

106
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,260
Mrs. Braverman must be out.

107
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:54,760
She could be out of town. Maybe she'll be gone for months.

108
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:59,040
By then, the cheesecake may have gone bad. We don't want her to come back to bad cheesecake.

109
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,020
No, that could kill her.

110
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,080
Well, we don't want that.

111
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,260
No, so we're protecting her.

112
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,020
Well, we should take it.

113
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,000
Yeah, but we should move quick.

114
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,320
Why?

115
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,080
Because I think I just heard her moving around in there.

116
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:08,740
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go.

117
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:15,260
Do you think that it's inappropriate to wear a white lacy dress to a wedding?

118
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:16,140
Yes.

119
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:17,180
Excellent.

120
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:23,560
Oh, my God, that's David.

121
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,380
David who?

122
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,380
David, the scientist guy, David, that I was in love with.

123
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:30,440
David who went to Russia and broke my heart, David.

124
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:31,920
Oh, my God.

125
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,320
Oh, you say someone's name and then they turn around.

126
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:37,640
Phoebe.

127
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:39,220
David.

128
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:44,240
What, what are you doing here?

129
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:45,520
Aren't you supposed to be in Russia?

130
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,920
Yeah, I'm just, I'm just in town for a conference.

131
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:51,140
God, you look phenomenal.

132
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:53,740
Well, yeah.

133
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,400
You look great, too.

134
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:58,060
Did you get a haircut?

135
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,780
Yeah, well, I got like 30 of them.

136
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:04,740
Um, look, I got a confession to make.

137
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:07,560
Um, I was hoping to run into you here.

138
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:09,100
I didn't know whether I should call or not.

139
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:11,540
You know, I was only in town for a few days and, you know,

140
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:14,260
I didn't want to intrude on your life or anything like that.

141
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:16,120
But I really wanted to see you.

142
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:18,800
But I didn't know if you wanted to see me.

143
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:22,120
Well, of course I would want to see you.

144
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:24,940
I, I think about you all the time.

145
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:27,840
Really? Because I think about you all the time.

146
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:32,280
I mean, there's a statue in Minsk that reminds me of you so much.

147
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,380
I mean, um, it's actually of Lenin.

148
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:37,300
Like, you know, at certain angles.

149
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:37,660
Yeah.

150
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,480
Anyway, do you want to have dinner, uh, tonight?

151
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,220
Yes.

152
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,220
Oh, no.

153
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:46,940
Oh, uh, what?

154
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,620
I can't. I can't believe I have plans. I can't.

155
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:50,860
Can you do it tomorrow night, though?

156
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,520
Uh, no. I, I have to go in a few hours.

157
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,660
I have to be on the red eye.

158
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:59,360
Well, listen, you know, next time you're in Minsk, uh...

159
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,360
Baby, can I talk to you for a second?

160
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:02,060
Uh-huh.

161
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:03,920
What are you doing?

162
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:05,900
Well, I have plans with Joey tonight.

163
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:07,420
So? He'll understand.

164
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:08,580
No, he won't.

165
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,140
And that's not even the point.

166
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:15,880
Monica, I made a whole speech about how you do not cancel plans with friends.

167
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:17,860
And now, you know what?

168
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:21,500
Just because, potentially, the love of my life comes back from Russia

169
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:24,460
just for one night, I, I should change my beliefs?

170
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,960
I should change my beliefs.

171
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:29,480
No. No.

172
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:32,200
No, if I don't have my principles, I don't have anything.

173
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,300
God, you are so strong.

174
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:38,020
Or I should rush through dinner with Joey and I could meet David at nine.

175
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,560
Oh, my God, that is so good.

176
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:45,780
I'm full.

177
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,560
And yet, I know if I stop eating this, I'll regret it.

178
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,000
Hey, what do you got there?

179
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,980
Oh, it's, um, it's tofu cake.

180
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:57,520
Do you want some?

181
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,360
What are you doing tonight?

182
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:05,820
Dude, dude.

183
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:08,640
Oh, sorry.

184
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,000
Uh, I got those plans with Phoebe.

185
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:11,320
What?

186
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:12,020
Oh, really?

187
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:14,180
Monica said she had a date at nine.

188
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:15,080
What?

189
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:15,740
Tonight?

190
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:17,300
That's what Monica said.

191
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,220
After she gave me that big speech?

192
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,980
She goes and makes a date with a guy on the same night she has plans with me?

193
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,700
I think she's trying to pull a fast one on Big Daddy.

194
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,380
Now, if you'll excuse me.

195
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:29,700
Dude, dude, dude.

196
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:32,540
If I took off my pants right now, how would you feel?

197
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:34,580
Like your cousin, Glenn.

198
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:43,060
Oh, here.

199
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,000
I think this is us.

200
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:47,720
Limited seating, my ass.

201
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,280
Let's just see who made the cut.

202
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:51,620
Hi.

203
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:52,320
Hi.

204
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:53,300
I'm Monica Geller.

205
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,440
How do you know the bride and groom?

206
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:56,620
Oh, I used to work with Franny.

207
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:57,760
Used to work with her.

208
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:58,880
Used to.

209
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,140
I'm her relative, but I didn't get invited.

210
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,260
A blood relative.

211
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:03,840
Blood.

212
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,200
Stop saying blood to strangers.

213
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:11,460
From the ages of seven to nine, we were inseparable.

214
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,280
Inseparable.

215
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,720
And I didn't even get invited to this.

216
00:13:13,940 --> 00:13:14,940
Then why are you here?

217
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,200
My brother's date.

218
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,260
I had a date, okay?

219
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,680
Joan Tedeschi.

220
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:21,900
The linguist.

221
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:24,760
So, how about you?

222
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:26,560
How do you know the happy couple?

223
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,980
We went to college with both of them.

224
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,060
And now we live next door.

225
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,260
Okay, you're fine.

226
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,360
You know, you would have liked Joan.

227
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:37,600
She's very pleasant.

228
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:40,300
There, there.

229
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:41,580
Her back looks like that.

230
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,280
That's not broad, is it?

231
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:49,800
Come on, Joey.

232
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:51,360
You've got to be ready to order by now.

233
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:52,660
You know what?

234
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:54,340
I don't think I like this table either.

235
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,500
Maybe we should move again.

236
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,820
No, we're staying right here.

237
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:57,460
Excuse me.

238
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:58,180
We're ready to order.

239
00:13:58,820 --> 00:13:59,780
I don't work here.

240
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,180
Well, then you shouldn't be walking around.

241
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:07,320
Hey.

242
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:07,860
Hi.

243
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:08,780
Are you guys ready yet?

244
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:09,380
Yeah, uh-huh.

245
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:12,100
I'm gonna have the green salad with the house dressing.

246
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,280
